# TypeScript & React Standards

- Functional components only; TypeScript for all new files (`.ts` / `.tsx`).
- **Arrow functions first** for components, hooks, and helpers (`export const X = () => …`). See `arrow-functions.mdc`.
- Named exports for components/hooks; default export allowed for pages and `App` (`const App = () => …; export default App`).
- Props: explicit types / interfaces; no `any`.
- Hooks: shared in `hooks/`, feature-local in `features/<name>/hooks/`.
- Side effects (fetch, storage) belong in `services/` or hooks — not in presentational UI.
- Keep components focused; extract when a file grows or logic mixes concerns.
- Match existing naming: `PascalCase` components, `camelCase` functions/hooks (`useX`), `kebab-case` CSS files if added.
